{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>They are clothed</b> — like \"with fat of flocks\" (the word being) many. And our predecessors of blessed memory interpreted it as a euphemism. And the correct in my eyes: that כרים is like כר נרחב (a broad tract), and the proof: \"and the valleys\"." "<b>They are enveloped</b> — from the root of המתעטף, like ילבשו. And יתרועעו from the root of תרועה, in the manner of \"the mountains and the hills shall break forth before you in song\"."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:48.486497815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}